  "description": "UPENAH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group I 2/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C75 H77 Dy5 N14 O20,5.5(C1 H4 O1),2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.647-4.238 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.50-136.05°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy5(L3)2(μ2-OCH3)(μ2-OH)2(μ4-O)(NO3)2(CH3OH)2]·6CH3OH·2CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
